#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""jev-scope-control: a PreToolUse hook for Claude Code and Codex, and the check behind the pi and opencode plugins.

Before an exec, write or edit tool call runs, ask Jev (TypeSafe's System One model) whether the
call is within the scope the user asked for or agreed to, explicitly or implicitly. If it isn't, deny
the call and tell the assistant why. See design/jev-scope-control-design.md.

Standard library only. Reads TYPESAFE_API_KEY from ~/.config/jev-scope-control/env, else from the
environment. Always exits 0 and fails open: any
error lets the call run.

The context sent to Jev: `task` (the user's last message), `conversation`, `actions`,
`earlier_actions`, `summary` and `sentences`. Before the call runs there is no reply, so `summary` is
empty. The call itself is added as `proposed_action`.

Claude Code and Codex send a PreToolUse event naming their transcript. The pi and opencode plugins
(pi/, opencode/) have no transcript file to name, so they send the context themselves,
{"host", "session_id", "task", "actions", "earlier_actions", "conversation"}, plus the call:
{"tool_name", "tool_input"}.
"""

